  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "$\\,$ $∃x\\in R,\\,$ ${x}^{2}=-1$\n\nWhich of the following expresses the statement given above?",
  "worked_solution": "The existential quantifier \"$∃$\" means \"there exists.\" So, our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $x\\in R$ **such that** ${x}^{2}=-1.$\n\nThis can be further simplified as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a real number whose square equals $-1.$\n\n**Note:** This statement is false.",
